## Why This Is Asked
Assess practical Azure devops, security, and data isolation in a beginner-friendly stack. The candidate must describe concrete steps, not abstractions.

## Key Concepts
- Function Apps, HTTP triggers, and binding to Cosmos DB
- Partition keys and per-tenant isolation in Cosmos DB SQL API
- Secrets management with Azure Key Vault and managed identities
- Per-environment configuration with Azure App Configuration
- GitHub Actions multi-environment deployment
- Testing: unit + integration (Cosmos DB Emulator)
- Cost control: Consumption plan, autoscale, budgets

## Code Example
```javascript
// index.js (Azure Function)
const { CosmosClient } = require('@azure/cosmos');
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const tenantId = (req.headers['x-tenant-id'] || req.query.tenantId);
  const client = new CosmosClient(process.env.COSMOS_CONNECTION_STRING);
  const container = client.database('TenantDB').container('Notes');
  const item = { id: req.body.id || require('uuid').v4(), tenantId, note: req.body.note };
  const { resource } = await container.items.create(item);
  context.res = { status: 201, body: resource };
};
```

